      "notes": "Corrected independent Horizon Strix Halo reproduction from internal NVMe-backed Btrfs storage. Exact STRIX base plus Q4_0 MTP draft head; Kyuz0 ROCmFP4 toolbox runtime b9219 / 1faa48eef / ROCm 7.2.4. Median of 3 measured runs after 1 warmup, using fixed cache-busting operator-style ~8K prompts shared across configurations, cache_prompt=false, greedy sampling (temperature 0/top_k 1), ignore_eos=true, and exactly 256 generated tokens. Native decode runs: 23.88, 23.22, 24.08 tok/s; median 23.88. Measured MTP acceptance: 0.567, 0.536, 0.567; median 0.567. No-MTP control was 13.34 tok/s, so n-max 3 improved decode by 78.95%; n-max 2 was 22.66 and n-max 4 was 21.86 tok/s. A pinned newer b9311 build regressed to 23.33 tok/s (23.50 with GPU_MAX_HW_QUEUES=2), so b9219 remains the best verified runtime. Internal cold readiness was 4.222 s. Publisher SHA256SUMS passed after relocation. A bounded Hermes operator workflow completed 9 tool calls, computed and matched SHA-256 and byte count, wrote a report, and read it back; final content was correct. The earlier external-drive measurements are superseded by this corrected internal-storage run.",
